    <section
        class="section alt"
        id="overview">

        <div class="container section-grid">

            <div>

                <span class="section-label">
                    Overview
                </span>

                <h2 class="section-title">
                    What I am building
                </h2>

            </div>


            <div class="content">

                <p>

                    The goal is to build a small processor where I can follow
                    an instruction from fetch and decode all the way through
                    the register file and execution hardware. The first version
                    supports a basic scalar ALU, and the next part adds SIMD so
                    one instruction can operate on four packed values in
                    parallel.

                </p>


                <p>

                    I am keeping the design small on purpose so I can understand
                    every block, simulate it separately, and then connect the
                    whole processor together before moving on to synthesis and
                    timing analysis.

                </p>

            </div>

        </div>

    </section>



    <section
        class="section"
        id="architecture">

        <div class="container section-grid">

            <div>

                <span class="section-label">
                    Architecture
                </span>

                <h2 class="section-title">
                    Current datapath
                </h2>

            </div>


            <div class="content">

                <p>

                    The processor starts with an 8-bit program counter. The
                    program counter selects a 16-bit instruction from instruction
                    memory, the decoder breaks the instruction into control and
                    register fields, and the register file provides two operands
                    to the execution hardware.

                </p>


                <div class="architecture">

                    <div class="flow">

                        <div class="flow-block">
                            Program Counter
                        </div>

                        <div class="flow-arrow">
                            ↓
                        </div>

                        <div class="flow-block">
                            Instruction Memory
                        </div>

                        <div class="flow-arrow">
                            ↓
                        </div>

                        <div class="flow-block">
                            Instruction Decoder
                        </div>

                        <div class="flow-arrow">
                            ↓
                        </div>

                        <div class="flow-block">
                            Register File
                        </div>

                        <div class="flow-arrow">
                            ↓
                        </div>


                        <div class="execution-grid">

                            <div class="execution-box">

                                <h3>
                                    Scalar ALU
                                </h3>

                                <div class="flow-block">
                                    16-bit ADD / SUB / AND / OR
                                </div>

                            </div>


                            <div class="execution-box">

                                <h3>
                                    SIMD Unit
                                </h3>

                                <div class="lanes">

                                    <div class="lane">
                                        Lane 3<br>4-bit
                                    </div>

                                    <div class="lane">
                                        Lane 2<br>4-bit
                                    </div>

                                    <div class="lane">
                                        Lane 1<br>4-bit
                                    </div>

                                    <div class="lane">
                                        Lane 0<br>4-bit
                                    </div>

                                </div>

                            </div>

                        </div>


                        <div class="flow-arrow">
                            ↓
                        </div>

                        <div class="flow-block">
                            Result Select + Register Writeback
                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>

    </section>



    <section
        class="section alt"
        id="instruction">

        <div class="container section-grid">

            <div>

                <span class="section-label">
                    Instruction
                </span>

                <h2 class="section-title">
                    16-bit format
                </h2>

            </div>


            <div class="content">

                <p>

                    I am currently using one bit to select scalar or SIMD
                    execution, three bits for the instruction class, three
                    register-address fields, and a three-bit function field.

                </p>


                <div class="instruction-wrap">

                    <div class="instruction">

                        <div>
                            <strong>SIMD</strong>
                            <span>[15]</span>
                        </div>

                        <div>
                            <strong>opcode</strong>
                            <span>[14:12]</span>
                        </div>

                        <div>
                            <strong>rd</strong>
                            <span>[11:9]</span>
                        </div>

                        <div>
                            <strong>rs1</strong>
                            <span>[8:6]</span>
                        </div>

                        <div>
                            <strong>rs2</strong>
                            <span>[5:3]</span>
                        </div>

                        <div>
                            <strong>func</strong>
                            <span>[2:0]</span>
                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>


                <p style="margin-top: 22px;">

                    The current ALU function codes are
                    <strong>000 = ADD</strong>,
                    <strong>001 = SUB</strong>,
                    <strong>010 = AND</strong>, and
                    <strong>011 = OR</strong>.
                    Bit 15 selects whether the operation uses the scalar or SIMD
                    execution path.

                </p>

            </div>

        </div>

    </section>



    <section
        class="section"
        id="rtl">

        <div class="container section-grid">

            <div>

                <span class="section-label">
                    RTL
                </span>

                <h2 class="section-title">
                    Main modules
                </h2>

            </div>


            <div class="content">

                <div class="module-list">

                    <div class="module">

                        <code>
                            alu.sv
                        </code>

                        <p>
                            16-bit combinational scalar ALU supporting ADD,
                            SUB, AND, and OR.
                        </p>

                    </div>


                    <div class="module">

                        <code>
                            regfile.sv
                        </code>

                        <p>
                            Eight 16-bit registers with two combinational read
                            ports, one synchronous write port, and R0 fixed at
                            zero.
                        </p>

                    </div>


                    <div class="module">

                        <code>
                            instruction_decoder.sv
                        </code>

                        <p>
                            Breaks the 16-bit instruction into register fields
                            and generates ALU, write-enable, SIMD, and validity
                            control signals.
                        </p>

                    </div>


                    <div class="module">

                        <code>
                            program_counter.sv
                        </code>

                        <p>
                            8-bit sequential program counter that resets to
                            zero and advances through instruction addresses.
                        </p>

                    </div>


                    <div class="module">

                        <code>
                            instruction_memory.sv
                        </code>

                        <p>
                            Stores the 16-bit instructions used to bring up and
                            test the processor.
                        </p>

                    </div>


                    <div class="module">

                        <code>
                            processor_top.sv
                        </code>

                        <p>
                            Connects the processor blocks into the complete
                            datapath. Scalar integration is being completed
                            before the SIMD result path is added.
                        </p>

                    </div>


                    <div class="module">

                        <code>
                            simd_lane.sv
                        </code>

                        <p>
                            Planned 4-bit lane that will implement the same
                            basic operations as the scalar ALU.
                        </p>

                    </div>


                    <div class="module">

                        <code>
                            simd_unit.sv
                        </code>

                        <p>
                            Planned four-lane execution block. All four lanes
                            receive the same operation while working on
                            different packed data.
                        </p>

                    </div>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>

    </section>



